  "reason": "Density relative to argon (~0.50) means molar mass ~20 g/mol (Ar=40). Binary compounds of three elements with two adjacent groups: likely B2H6 (diborane, molar mass 27.7) and C2H2 (acetylene, molar mass 26) or similar? But density ~0.5 of Ar gives ~20 g/mol, so maybe NH3 (17) and CH4 (16)? However, NH3 is soluble and basic, CH4 insoluble. But they are binary compounds of three elements? Actually NH3 and CH4 are binary (two elements each). The question says 'binary compounds consisting of three elements' - likely means each gas is a binary compound (two elements) but together they contain three elements. So A=NH3 (soluble, pH>7), B=CH4 (insoluble). Combustion: 4NH3+3O2→2N2+6H2O; CH4+2O2→CO2+2H2O. Products: N2 (28), H2O (18*6=108), CO2 (44), H2O (36) total=216? But sum with coefficients: 2N2+6H2O+CO2+2H2O = 2*28+6*18+44+2*18=56+108+44+36=244. Range 230-250. So A.",
  "choice": "A"
}
